<title>UK: Tomkins says to pay final div as FID.</title>
<headline>Tomkins says to pay final div as FID.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British diversified industrial group Tomkins Plc said on Friday it would pay its final dividend in the form of foreign income dividend.</p>
<p>The company had proposed a final dividend of 8.39 pence (net) per ordinary share for the financial year 1997/98.</p>
<p>The company said it had decided to pay it in the form FID after the UK's Labour government made changes in advance corporation tax in its budget.</p>
